#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:5
#: 675aa1c239aa4b4d916bad43cb752bfc
msgid "Nooploop for Non-GPS Navigation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:9
#: d35b2047df3242fc9f29f1f577246058
msgid "This article explains how a `Nooploop <https://www.nooploop.com/en/>`__ system based on UWB(Ultra Wide Band) technology can be used as a short-range substitute for a GPS allowing position control modes like Loiter, PosHold, RTL, Auto indoors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:12
#: 00a94a79f6244e3ba294a4ac7c286926
msgid "Required Hardware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:14
#: 8a951721cc9e4f549eae9ef81149c625
msgid "5 Nooploop LinkTrack nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:15
#: d9e50bfd78064123a87f77781d1ed3a0
msgid "one `Arduino Nano Every <https://store.arduino.cc/usa/nano-every>`__ (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:16
#: ca8bef4a34144c96a2009defecde8576
msgid "4 `portable chargers <https://www.amazon.com/s/ref=nb_sb_noss_2?url=search-alias%3Daps&field-keywords=portable+charger&rh=i%3Aaps%2Ck%3Aportable+charger>`__ with type A USB ports to power the anchors (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:17
#: 84f6482590434f54aec90789aaaa4e2e
msgid "4 `tripods <https://www.amazon.com/s/ref=nb_sb_noss_1?url=search-alias%3Daps&field-keywords=tripod&rh=i%3Aaps%2Ck%3Atripod>`__ to mount the anchors (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:20
#: fa354b7619d541e7a2ea0457d24a716d
msgid "Preparing the anchors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:22
#: f9b7606eb081428394cad7acb367ef86
msgid "4 Nooploop nodes need to be configured to act as anchors. Follow Nooploop `LinkTrack user manual <https://www.nooploop.com/en/download/>`__ to setup and calibrate them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:25
#: 6f8842fde35d44bb9feef30c66a1324b
msgid "Placing the anchors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:27
#: 4b074a94476942778ecba2912e7058aa
msgid "The anchors should be placed in a rectangular shape. Anchor 0 will act as \"origin\" and Y axis of Nooploop system will act as \"North\". The configuration is slightly simpler if the line from anchor 0 to anchor 1 is due North but it is not required as the :ref:`BCN_ORIENT_YAW <BCN_ORIENT_YAW>` parameter can be used to account this difference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:33
#: c43760d9a14d4adf8f8feb6f00524641
msgid "Preparing the tag"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:35
#: d17c2942f7be4965bd2e197c785d19b6
msgid "Use Nooploop NAssistant tool to configure one node to act as a tag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:37
#: 33e6525d73814c9e9d9e10d9651b1b1e
msgid "set Protocol to Node_Frame2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:38
#: 8ab86081bb5f42499391b9c71f0794cd
msgid "set Baudrate to 921600"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:39
#: ebde43b95d4844c3b78e635e492cb208
msgid "set Update Rate to 25"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:40
#: 1ac977ea002d431c9b8867f5148b384c
msgid "set Filter Factor to 0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:46
#: 98dae3f239b848cdbc54c1733585ea46
msgid "Connecting the tag to the Flight Controller"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:48
#: a0bb427bc6aa4de6aa8a2605c8769c45
msgid "It is possible to directly connect UART port of the tag to the FC. However, UART Tx of certain FCs is not compatible with Nooploop UART Rx (According to developers at Nooploop, it seems to be caused by a CP2012 inside Nooploop nodes. It is possible that this problem can be solved by removing this CP2012). It causes the FC to be unable to communicate with the tag. Pixhawk 4 mini and Kakute F7 are confirmed to have this issue. In this case, an Arduino Nano Every can be used as a work-around. Use Ardnio IDE to upload `Nooploop work-around sketch <https://github.com/chobitsfan/nooploop_workaround.git>`__ to a Arduino Nano Every and connect its UART Tx to UART Rx of the tag. For the following we assume that the tag is connected to the FC's UART port corresponding to SERIAL1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:54
#: 53de161dced04b55b66a64afa9208c19
msgid "Configuration through the Ground Station"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:56
#: 965508df053d4613b5d10e7df042b93c
msgid "Ensure that Copter is loaded onto the autopilot and connect with a Ground Station (i.e. Mission Planner)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:58
#: 2eb73bb7afc64dda871fe241cce3a114
msgid "set :ref:`BCN_TYPE <BCN_TYPE>` to 3 (means using Nooploop system)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:59
#: 09e7195a20794ce0b07f7b05f0148b11
msgid "set :ref:`BCN_LATITUDE <BCN_LATITUDE>`, :ref:`BCN_LONGITUDE <BCN_LONGITUDE>` and :ref:`BCN_ALT <BCN_ALT>` to match your actual location.  Getting these values exactly correct is not particularly important although getting them close is required in order for the compass's declination to be correctly looked up from the database held within ArduPilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:60
#: 7cc0e24d7ee64dfc907e87276d267ad3
msgid "set :ref:`BCN_ORIENT_YAW <BCN_ORIENT_YAW>` to the heading from the origin anchor to the 2nd anchor.  One way to capture this value is to stand at the origin holding the vehicle so that its nose points towards the second beacon.  Read the vehicle's heading from the HUD and enter this value into :ref:`BCN_ORIENT_YAW <BCN_ORIENT_YAW>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:61
#: c986fc0e50bd4e34baf01016b0407d0d
msgid "set :ref:`EK3_BCN_DELAY <EK3_BCN_DELAY>` to 20"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:62
#: b13398201cd445218ce07a1fb03be779
msgid "set :ref:`EK3_SRC1_POSXY <EK3_SRC1_POSXY>` to 4 (\"Beacon\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:63
#: 3239f0a02fcb446ca82619ffdc43cbdb
msgid "set :ref:`EK3_SRC1_POSZ <EK3_SRC1_POSZ>` to 4 (\"Beacon\") to use NoopLoop for altitude or leave at \"1\" to use the barometer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:64
#: eaeddc488153457b9aa4f73aa49012f0
msgid "set :ref:`EK3_SRC1_VELXY <EK3_SRC1_VELXY>` to 0 (\"None\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:65
#: da9a58dc11324dbf9ca29c3d1dd18996
msgid "set :ref:`EK3_SRC1_VELZ <EK3_SRC1_VELZ>` to 0 (\"None\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:66
#: d785baf0c1574447a13adbc9a2eb468d
msgid "set :ref:`EK3_SRC1_YAW<EK3_SRC1_YAW>` to 1 (\"Compass\") since a compass must be used in conjunction with this device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:67
#: ce2f17faa889404c9ac17fd15fab3c86
msgid "set :ref:`GPS1_TYPE <GPS1_TYPE>` to 0 to disable the GPS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:68
#: b305ce3147d24d84957636b56ad3345a
msgid "set :ref:`ARMING_SKIPCHK <ARMING_SKIPCHK>` to 8 to disable the GPS arming check"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:69
#: b6f8cc09c3f748098b373a7deff2ed3e
msgid "set :ref:`SERIAL1_BAUD <SERIAL1_BAUD>` to 921 to set SERIAL1's baud rate to 921600"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:70
#: 2072ed29066c4bdaaaba63c54ad5e18d
msgid "set :ref:`SERIAL1_PROTOCOL <SERIAL1_PROTOCOL>` to 13 to enable reading the IndoorLoiter2 protocol"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:71
#: 9f46d7e0b0dc45e8b185d00b6cfb4746
msgid "set :ref:`BRD_SER1_RTSCTS <BRD_SER1_RTSCTS>` to 0 to ensure SERIAL1 does not use flow control, assuming it has this capability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:74
#: 4cd0a69cc19e42c3a710110a762be26a
msgid "Ground Testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:76
#: 8a0604d5e980493bad81fc06f66bd6c3
msgid "Connect the Autopilot to a ground station."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:77
#: fd76686801094754bd9033537eb95fbd
msgid "After about 1 minute the vehicle's position should jump to the latitude, longitude you input during the configuration step (above)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:78
#: 87efc3b6b0cf4702a9cc3811f2560f8a
msgid "Check that the vehicle's position is relatively stable (i.e. moving around less than one meter)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:79
#: fd0eef2af29f4b2ba98bad5d7dd7d3d6
msgid "Walk the vehicle around between the anchors and ensure that its position on the map updates correctly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:82
#: de63da20dda94b228b4e034eb4769b2d
msgid "Flight testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:84
#: f63adbb5154a421b96e6c9174b74b94c
msgid "Setup the transmitter with Stabilize, AltHold and Loiter flight modes. Take off in AltHold mode and maintain a stable hover. Switch to Loiter but be ready to switch back to AltHold or Stabilize if the vehicle's position or altitude becomes unstable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:89
#: 592fc218d43f4feca7e818510f641edd
msgid "DataFlash logging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-nooploop.rst:91
#: 69803486b6144f779e8cf1344c2da257
msgid "The distance to the beacons can be found in the dataflash log's BCN message's D0, D1, D2, D3 fields."
msgstr ""
